# The versions of the gate tools, in one place: check.sh installs each at its pin and runs it, on
# every machine and in CI, reading NAME=value lines with nothing else on the line. A Go tool's
# value is a module version, such as v1.2.3, which check.sh builds with go install. shellcheck and
# zizmor are no Go modules: each one's line is its release, and the lines after it the SHA-256 of
# that release's archive for each system the gate runs on, which check.sh downloads and checks
# before unpacking. The weekly tool-pins workflow compares each pin with the newest release (the
# Go module proxy's, or the tool's GitHub releases), opening an issue when one is behind. A pin
# moves here, by the developer's hand, in a pull request he reads: a gate's tools change only when
# we change something (developer, 2026-10-14). A change to this file runs the full check matrix.
